sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    %% PKI Issuing CA System - Revocation and CRL Publication Sequence
    
    actor Requester as Cert Owner / Security Officer
    participant Gateway as API Gateway / Spring Security
    participant RevSvc as RevocationService
    participant CrlSvc as CrlService
    participant HSM as Pkcs11HsmAdapter
    participant DB as MySQL Database
    participant FS as Public File Store (/crl)
    participant RP as Relying Party (Browser / Client)

    Requester->>Gateway: POST /api/v1/certificates/{serialNumber}/revoke<br/>{reasonCode: "keyCompromise", comments: "Stolen"}
    Gateway->>RevSvc: revokeCertificate(serialNumber, reason, comments, userId)
    
    rect rgb(255, 240, 245)
        Note over RevSvc,DB: Atomic Database Transaction
        RevSvc->>DB: UPDATE certificates SET status='REVOKED' WHERE serial_number=...
        RevSvc->>DB: INSERT INTO revocation_records (serial, reason, date, initiated_by)
        RevSvc->>DB: INSERT INTO audit_events ('CERTIFICATE_REVOKED') with HMAC chain
    end
    RevSvc-->>Gateway: 200 OK (Status: REVOKED)
    Gateway-->>Requester: 200 OK
    
    Note over CrlSvc: Automated Cron or On-Demand Trigger
    CrlSvc->>CrlSvc: initiateCrlGeneration()
    CrlSvc->>DB: SELECT * FROM revocation_records WHERE ca_id=...
    DB-->>CrlSvc: Active revocation list
    
    CrlSvc->>CrlSvc: Construct X509v2CRLBuilder (thisUpdate, nextUpdate, CRLNumber)
    CrlSvc->>HSM: signCrl(crlBuilder, caKeyAlias)
    Note over HSM: Signs CRL inside HSM token boundary
    HSM-->>CrlSvc: Signed X509CRL object
    
    CrlSvc->>DB: INSERT INTO crl_records (crl_number, this_update, next_update, pem)
    CrlSvc->>FS: Write binary DER file to /var/www/pki/crl/issuing-ca.crl
    CrlSvc->>FS: Write PEM file to /var/www/pki/crl/issuing-ca.crl.pem
    
    Note over RP: Relying party verifies client certificate
    RP->>FS: HTTP GET /crl/issuing-ca.crl
    FS-->>RP: Returns latest signed binary CRL
    RP->>RP: Independently checks if serialNumber is in CRL
